      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "REGALADE (1) came from last at one stage to get up for second in an impressive form reversal over 1200m at Warren last start. Nicely placed over the extra 100m and in a race of questionable quality he gets his chance to break through. BAULKHAM HILLS (7) had the first run back from a six-month spell for a new stable last time out and was just fair in finishing sixth over 1200m. Lightly raced mare who will take a lot from that run and can play a bigger role this afternoon. DISTANT STRIPES (5) placed on three consecutive occasions before failing on a heavy track at Wagga most recently. Deserves another chance. BANGELZ (2) appreciated the drop in grade when a closing third over 1200m at Cowra last start. That was her first run in a month so there is more improvement to come. BLOOMIN' HELL (8) returned from a spell with an eye-catching second at Narromine six weeks ago. Nicely drawn and should be competitive again.",
